{title: Yankee Doodle}
{artist: Traditional, 18th century}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, kids}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Yankee Doodle went to [D]town
[G]A-riding on a [D]pony
[G]Stuck a feather [C]in his cap
And [D]called it maca[G]roni

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Yankee Doodle, keep it up
[G]Yankee Doodle dandy
[C]Mind the music and the step
And [G]with the [D]girls be [G]handy

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Father and I went down to [D]camp
[G]Along with Captain [D]Gooding
And [G]there we saw the [C]men and boys
As [D]thick as hasty [G]pudding

{chorus}
